From: Fuad Tabba <tabba@google.com>
Date: Thu Jul 16 17:01:17 2026 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] ANDROID: KVM: arm64: Fix mp_state read in pkvm_vcpu_init_psci()

The 2026-04 pick of "Remove MP state tracking from EL2" is the
android14-6.1 variant and lacks the android15-6.6 hunks that pass the
host-requested mp_state into pkvm_vcpu_init_psci(). The field the
function still reads is no longer written anywhere and always reads 0
(KVM_MP_STATE_RUNNABLE), so every vCPU of a pvmfw VM takes the RUNNABLE
path: the second fails to claim the primary slot, and the WARN_ON()
around the call panics the hypervisor. Any pvmfw VM with more than one
vCPU crashes the device on its first run.

Pass mp_state from init_pkvm_hyp_vcpu() as android15-6.6 does.

Fixes: 6d7738d210628 ("ANDROID: KVM: arm64: Remove MP state tracking from EL2")
Bug: 534667741
Change-Id: Icb9215eca831f7c574e51135c925130dc8d3f7ab
Signed-off-by: Fuad Tabba <tabba@google.com>
(cherry picked from commit c300c987659ff7139a73b048c428001e25044367)
Signed-off-by: Lee Jones <joneslee@google.com>

[gki6677 reshape note - 2026-11-02, Z.ai]
Reshaped for the 6.6.77 pin: hunks 1-2 (signature + mp_state source)
apply verbatim; the call-site hunk re-anchors on the pin's older
error-path form (ret = pkvm_vcpu_init_psci(...) followed by goto
done, not upstream's WARN_ON one-liner); upstream's 4th hunk
(blank-line removal inside pvm_psci_vcpu_off(), a region
restructured by later commits relative to the pin) is cosmetic and
dropped. Semantics at the pin are unchanged - init_pkvm_hyp_vcpu()
already holds the race-free host mp_state local (pkvm.c:706/730)
that this fix threads through, so the change ships for
upstream-shape consistency and future backport-drift reduction.
Verified: strict git apply on the pin replica.

Origin: android.googlesource.com/kernel/common 06cf7e02a104e882bc3f439b8b573b97e810afdc
Batch: B-2 (P4 kvm/pKVM cluster) - Class B, RESHAPED for the pin; predicted ABI delta zero

---
diff --git a/arch/arm64/kvm/hyp/nvhe/pkvm.c b/arch/arm64/kvm/hyp/nvhe/pkvm.c
index f7ed70d64..f9227d070 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/kvm/hyp/nvhe/pkvm.c
+++ b/arch/arm64/kvm/hyp/nvhe/pkvm.c
@@ -558,12 +558,12 @@ static int pkvm_vcpu_init_ptrauth(struct pkvm_hyp_vcpu *hyp_vcpu)
 	return ret;
 }
 
-static int pkvm_vcpu_init_psci(struct pkvm_hyp_vcpu *hyp_vcpu)
+static int pkvm_vcpu_init_psci(struct pkvm_hyp_vcpu *hyp_vcpu, u32 mp_state)
 {
 	struct vcpu_reset_state *reset_state = &hyp_vcpu->vcpu.arch.reset_state;
 	struct pkvm_hyp_vm *hyp_vm = pkvm_hyp_vcpu_to_hyp_vm(hyp_vcpu);
 
-	if (hyp_vcpu->vcpu.arch.mp_state.mp_state == KVM_MP_STATE_STOPPED) {
+	if (mp_state == KVM_MP_STATE_STOPPED) {
 		reset_state->reset = false;
 		hyp_vcpu->power_state = PSCI_0_2_AFFINITY_LEVEL_OFF;
 	} else if (pkvm_hyp_vm_has_pvmfw(hyp_vm)) {
@@ -751,7 +751,7 @@ static int init_pkvm_hyp_vcpu(struct pkvm_hyp_vcpu *hyp_vcpu,
 	if (ret)
 		goto done;
 
-	ret = pkvm_vcpu_init_psci(hyp_vcpu);
+		ret = pkvm_vcpu_init_psci(hyp_vcpu, mp_state);
 	if (ret)
 		goto done;
 
